{
  "reason": "Use a Tier 2 change: separate prediction-aligned final-mask training from auxiliary history corruption. Increasing negatives and adding relative biases failed to exceed 0.5800, while recent-item fusion recovered only part of the loss; this supports testing a different representation issue rather than adding more capacity. Currently, auxiliary masking removes historical context from the final query during training, whereas inference supplies intact history, potentially weakening both the Transformer and recent-item path.",
  "module": [
    "data_processing_and_feature_engineering",
    "training_evaluation"
  ],
  "plan": {
    "data_processing_and_feature_engineering": "Modify MaskedHistories to produce two views of the same sampled training prefix: a clean-context view with only its final target masked, and the existing corrupted view containing auxiliary historical masks. Construct the clean view before historical corruption so its visible context matches prediction_sequence; keep the final target hidden in both views and exclude its label from auxiliary supervision. Preserve supplied splits, prefix sampling, sequence lengths, item IDs, existing sequence and labels variables, and prediction_sequence(history, itemnum, maxlen); add clean_sequence to the Dataset return tuple and update its consumer. This isolates training-context mismatch without changing inference inputs or accessing validation items during training.",
    "model_design": null,
    "training_evaluation": "Run clean_sequence and sequence through the same MaskedSASRec instance and replace the existing objective with 0.5 times clean-view final-target cross-entropy plus 0.5 times corrupted-view auxiliary-mask cross-entropy, using clean final-target loss alone when no auxiliary masks exist. Preserve the shared 1024-negative draw, collision masking, tied embeddings, learned bias, relative attention, recent-item fusion, optimizer, hyperparameters, seeds, checkpoint selection, and category time limits so context separation is the single experimental change. Preserve train_one, evaluate, make_validation, write_predict_script, DATA_DIR=os.environ['GAGC_DATA_DIR'], trial-local artifacts, all four routes, and the predictor signature; inference continues loading exactly one selected checkpoint per category and executing one model forward pass. Verify clean-view construction against prediction_sequence, hidden-target exclusion, finite gradients, and strict checkpoint reload, then compare authoritative macro validation HR@10 against 0.5675 and the historical 0.5800 best without accessing test files or generating a substitute submission."
  }
}
